<< {"id":4,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{"text":"JETCARP won't start or show scenes in the background host until its photosensitive seizure warning has been accepted.\n\nPHOTOSENSITIVE SEIZURE WARNING\n\nJETCARP's animations can flash and flicker rapidly, and can trigger seizures in people with photosensitive epilepsy.\n\nSome rules change most of the screen every generation. A rule with B0, for example, turns the whole field over at each step. Run fast, full screen or as the desktop background, such a rule can flicker many times a second.\n\nFlashing like this can also trigger a seizure, occasionally, in someone with no history of seizures.\n\nIf you feel dizzy, or notice altered vision, eye or muscle twitching, disorientation or any involuntary movement, stop at once, look away from the screen, and see a doctor.\n\nTo read it and answer, open the JETCARP app, or run `jetcarp setup` in a terminal. Without a terminal, `jetcarp setup --yes --seizure-warning no-disorder` records that you don't have epilepsy or a seizure disorder.","type":"text"}],"isError":true,"resultType":"complete"}}
